🟢 **F-1601-1** (s1601 2026-08-09, MEASURED AND PARTLY DISCHARGED THIS FIRE — A THIRD OF THE OWNER'S DESK IS NOT WAITING ON THE OWNER, AND THAT IS WHY THE BOARD READ DRY FOR FIVE CONSECUTIVE FIRES). Found by auditing the desk I inherited instead of carrying it. ⚠️ **THE HEADER'S OWN WORDS ARE FALSE FOR A THIRD OF WHAT IT COUNTS.** The handoff declares `🔺 OWNER'S DESK — 31 awaiting a word`. ✓ **MEASURED by reading the GATE clause of all 28 desk findings plus the 3 blocked slugs, one row at a time — not grepped, because the gate is free prose and a grep reports its hits and never its misses.** The 31 split three ways: **19 genuinely turn on a word** (12 direct owner words, 2 dependent on another finding's owner ruling — F-1532-2 on F-1167-1, F-1528-3 on F-1499-2 —, 2 attended-or-owner, 3 `blocked` slugs all `owner-fork`); **9 name a WORK ACT no owner can supply** — a measurement, a doc line, a code edit, a lane run; and **2 state in their own text that nothing is owed at all**: F-1589-3 (*"GATE: none owed; re-measure if it reddens in isolation"*) and F-1588-1 (*"GATE: none — this is a confirming measurement, not a defect. Non-blocking, no cure owed"*). 🔑 **THOSE LAST TWO CAN NEVER LEAVE THE DESK.** They are informational records parked in a queue whose only exit is an owner word they explicitly do not want. This is **F-1383-1's shape one level up**: that finding split `status:"blocked"` into `owner-fork` vs `gate-side` precisely because an overloaded refusal parks a fire-liftable hold in front of the owner forever — the desk overloads the same way, and has no `blockClass` to save it. ⭐ **THE EXPENSIVE HALF IS THE 9, AND IT IS THE DRY BOARD SEEN FROM THE OTHER SIDE.** s1597–s1600 each declared **PIPELINE-DRY ×4 (needs spec/owner)** and authored nothing, while these sat on the desk labelled owner debt: **F-1587-2** (a warming step or a named-cause timeout) · **F-1591-1** (the Arm 0 clamp table) · **F-1589-2** (a re-snapshot or a staleness warning) · **F-1588-2** (merge two refusal paths, or document the ordering) · **F-1587-1** (re-measure per project) · **F-1507-1** (show both shells on one node version) · **F-1510-1** (two named tests green at `--workers=1`) · **F-1536-2** (bucket the 66 `save/*` refs) · **F-DOOR-6** (a door-doc slice lands (a)+(b); only (c) is owner-optional). **Four of those nine say inside their own row that a fire or a doc line may take them** — F-DOOR-5 and F-E2S-3 likewise offer a `§7.4` arm while their forks stay owner-gated. A dry board and a 31-item desk are not two facts; they are one fact filed under the wrong heading. ✅ **PROVED BY TAKING ONE, NOT BY ARGUING IT: F-1587-1 IS CURED THIS FIRE** (see its row) — measured, mechanised, guarded, committed, **no owner word involved**, in a single fire that began by being told the board was dry. That is the claim's control: if these were really owner debt, that could not have happened. 📐 **WHAT I AM NOT CLAIMING:** I did not re-price the 19, and the genuine owner forks are untouched and still owed — the desk is not "mostly noise", it is **~61% real and mis-sized by ~39%**. Nor is the count itself wrong: 31 items ARE carried, and `desk-state-audit --status` correctly returns `CLOSED=0 · OPEN=4 · OPEN-DESK-ONLY=27 · UNRECORDED=0` — **nothing carried should have been dropped.** The defect is not the arithmetic, it is the WORD "awaiting", which asserts a routing that a third of the items contradict in their own closing sentence. ➡️ **THE CHEAP CURE, RECOMMENDED AND DELIBERATELY NOT BUILT THIS FIRE:** give `scripts/desk-state-audit.mjs` a `gateClass` column — `owner-word` / `work-act` / `none-owed` — failing safe to `owner-word` on anything unrecognised, exactly as `blockClass` does, since the dangerous direction is routing a real fork to a fire. ⛔ **I did not write it, on purpose:** classifying free prose by heuristic at the tail of a fire is how a fragile classifier gets born, and the 9 are listed **by name above**, so the next dry-board fire needs no mechanism to