dinate anyway, because the act of committing their own row is what moved the line they had just correctly read. **The factory's whole epistemic apparatus — VERIFY-DON'T-INHERIT, re-derive, cite at source — points backwards at claims you received. Nothing points forward at the claim you are about to emit into a file you are simultaneously changing.** ➡️ **The rule I'd hand forward: never cite a line number in a file your own commit touches — cite content, which survives the commit. And the general form: when you are both the observer and the editor, your measurement is stale the moment you save.** ⚠️ **The confirming detail is that I nearly shipped it too: my first cure asserted an anchor matched "exactly one row" when it matched two, and only a count I ran before committing caught it.** s1350 committed an instance of the class it discovered; s1351 did; s1352 caught its own with one command. **The defence was never insight — it was running the check on your own output, which is the one place insight does not reach.**
753:- **s1295 handoff (line-1 archive):** Last updated: 2026-07-31T18:00Z s1295 handoff, lock CLEARED — 🥇 **(A) THE SLICE THE LAST FIRE DELIBERATELY HELD HAD ALREADY SHIPPED, AND EVERY PROBE THAT FIRE HAD WAS STRUCTURALLY INCAPABLE OF SEEING IT (F-1295-1).** I set out to run s1294's §D(1) — the F-1294-2 control — and my harness **aborted on its own assertion**: `ARM MISMATCH: wanted MERGED, tree is CONTROL`, because `git checkout lane/e2-arsenal -- <the 4 slice paths>` produced **zero change**. ⭐ **That is the whole finding, and it was a mechanical guard rather than an insight that surfaced it: main already held the slice.** Verified by **blob hash at three refs**, never by diff — `PermissionLadder.ts 9451c000` · `ToolSurface.ts eb31d683` · `m4-01 5b674014` · `m4-05 b1cca7d1`, all **byte-identical to the lane**. They landed in **`b37c1fc6`, 16:59:12**, *thirteen minutes before* the s1294 handoff that says **"main was never modified"** — a **concurrent attended session's** commit titled ***"rehearsal round 2 launched (shipped pipeline, vein-hunter card)"***, whose broad `git add` swept up the four paths s1294 had checked out into main's working tree **in order to gate them**. Its `--stat` is *exactly* those four plus one BACKLOG line; **its message names none of them.** 🔑 **WHY THE VERIFICATION COULD NOT WORK — the half worth keeping.** s1294 reverted with `git checkout HEAD -- <paths>` and confirmed `git status` clean. Both are the textbook steps and **both were blind, because `HEAD` had itself moved**: the "revert" restored *from* the contaminated HEAD and therefore restored the slice, and the clean status was **caused by** the sweep rather than disproving it. ⚠️ **Generalised: a sweep's signature is the ABSENCE of dirt.** `git status`, `main..branch` (still 1 ahead, by the runner's own commit), a clean worktree — **all return identical answers whether the revert worked or the content was committed out from under it.** The only discriminating probe is a blob-hash comparison against a **pre-sweep ref**. ⚖️ **THE CLASS IS KNOWN AND THIS MEMBER INVERTS IT.** The ledger already carries *an `-A` commit swallows a live fire's work* — **authorship**. This one is **policy: work a fire deliberately REFUSED to merge got merged anyway.** A `HOLD` verdict lives in a review file and a goal leaf and **nothing in git defends it**; an **owner-BLOCKED** slice would ship through the same window, which is the version that costs a design fork. 🔒 **Scope proven, not assumed: every main commit since s1294's lock audited for `src/`+`e2e/` content — `b37c1fc6` is the ONLY one carrying code.** ➡️ **Free standing cure, adopted this fire: never check foreign content into MAIN's tree to gate it — gate in a detached worktree.** Mistake #12 already routes attribution runs there for *contention*; this extends it to *custody*, which is the stronger reason. ✅ **(B) THE CONTROL RAN PROPERLY AND THE SLICE IS CLEAN — F-1294-2 CLOSED, `agent-rung-honest-gate-v2` FORMALISED.** The arms s1294 specified (clean-main vs merged) **no longer exist**, so I measured the ones that answer the same question: **PRE-sweep (`00e4c074` blobs) vs POST-sweep (`HEAD` blobs)**, arm identity asserted **by blob hash before every single run**. In a **detached worktree** (never main's tree — a concurrent writer was still committing at 17:20 and 17:26), `--workers=1`, scratch port **5241**, **interleaved per spec** with **round 2 order-reversed**. **12 runs: `ap-standing-orders` PRE 0/2 red vs POST 0/2 · `ss-01-beats` PRE 2/2 vs POST 2/2 · `trail-guide-beat-priority` PRE 0/2 vs POST 0/2 — ALL EQUAL.** ⭐ **The box was NOT idle and that is fine — load fell 41.33 → 10.86 underneath, and interleaving converts drift into shared-mode noise.** The asymmetry that makes it usable at any load: **a red on the PRE arm cannot have been caused by the slice**, so heavy load raises the chance of a decisive exoneration and cannot manufacture a false one. Gates re-run on current main: **tsc clean · build rc=0 1.71 s · all 5 `test:node-guards` steps rc=0** (`agent-rung-conformance` 10/10 by TAP). Leaf → `merged`, `mergeHash b37c1fc6ca…` **with the irregular provenance stated ON the leaf rather than laundered into a normal-looking drain**; done-move retired `drained-s1295-b37c1fc6-…`; lane tip preserved as `archive/lane-c-s1295-absorbed-tip`; **GZ-01 item written** (real player-visible change). ⓘ **A guard caught me: I first wrote the short hash and `goal-tracker` red on `/^[0-9a-f]{40}$/`.** Worth recording because it is the cheap direction of the same lesson — the guard was right and I was fast. 🔬 **(C) F-1295-2 — ONE OF THE THREE "UNATTRIBUTED" REDS WAS A DOCUMENTED 34.1% FLAKE ALL ALONG, HIDDEN BY A HELPER-VS-TEST COORDINATE.** `logs/suite-red-inventory.md` row 24 records **this exact test** at **15/44 (34.1%) desktop AND 15/44 (34.1%) mobile** under `ss-01-beats.spec.ts:88`. **`:88` is the assertion inside the shared `expectBeat` HELPER; `:103` is the `test(` line Playwright reports as the location.** The control's raw output carries the inventory's reason **verbatim** (`expect(locator).toHaveAttribute(expected) failed`) *and* s1294's observed value **verbatim** (`unexpected value "ledger-page:town_elder"`) — one red, quoted at two depths. s1294 searched by the reporter's coordinate and correctly found nothing. ⓘ **I first wrote this row down as "corroboration at test level, not a verbatim fingerprint" and the control upgraded it** — the caution was right to record and wrong to keep. 💡 **The inventory is keyed by `file:line`, so every row rots the moment a spec gains a line above its test — silently and ONE-DIRECTIONALLY: it can only ever turn a known red into a mystery red.** That is a standing tax on every drain that triages against it; it wants a title column. **Fire-authorable.** 🧾 **(D) DUTIES.** **DEPLOY ATTEMPTED AND DENIED — THIRTEENTH CONSECUTIVE** (s1283→s1295); `bash scripts/deploy.sh` is not in the allowlist and I did **NOT** route it via `Bash(node: