the newsie release"*; **both restored to pre-arm SHA-256**, and the branch diff is **exactly one file** (`e2e/gazette-welcome.spec.ts`, +47/−7), which is itself the proof arm A's `src/` mutation was reverted. `drain-block-check` **CLEAR**. (2) **`lane-prime-env`** landed 17:08 (lane-a) — untriaged by me. (3) **lane-d still live** on `lane-run-tape`. (4) `066-walk8-engine:208` is a **half-done rename** decaying into a standing known-red that has now cost three batteries an explanation — fire-authorable scoped test repair. (5) **Do NOT re-run the workers experiment** (F-1293-1 closed it; F-1270-3's 1-vs-1 trap). (6) ⚠️ **My §E is a hypothesis like every §E before it.** 🔺 **OWNER DESK — ONE NEW ITEM, AND IT IS A COORDINATION RULING, NOT A BUG.** ⓘ **NEW (F-1295-1): an attended session and a fire disagreed about whether a slice shipped, and the attended won silently, because a broad `git add` outranks a review file.** The fire-side cure (gate in a detached worktree) is free and **already adopted**, so nothing is owed you technically. The question is only whether attended work should say so in the commit when it wants a fire's held slice — and whether path-scoped adds are worth the habit while a fire holds the lock. **RECOMMENDATION: one line of policy, no task.** 🔺 **STILL THE CHEAPEST: F-1279-2 — is `auto_repair` L1 or L2?** Recommendation **L2**, matching the ratified ladder line; the rung slice shipped with it firewalled at **1**, so this is now the only unruled row that merged work left behind. 🔺 **F-1101-1 / `calibrate-suite-workers-v2` — RETIRE THE THREAD** (s1294's ask; the box remedies buy nothing). 🔺 **F-1120-2 option (1b)** — ship `contact-sheets` (9.51 MB) *plus* the 0.15 MB of provenance; root cause one line away in **F-1193-2**. 🔺 F-1287-1 + F-1286-2 need an idle-machine rate · 🔺 **AP-07** · 🔺 plist `ProcessType` (F-1270-4) · 🔺 F-1267-3 · 🔺 F-1242-1 + F-1193-2 · 🔺 F-1260-3 · 🔺 F-1252-1 · 🔺 F-1257-4 · 🔺 F-1255-4/1 · 🔺 F-1254-3 · 🔺 F-1253-1/2/3 · 🔺 **F-1162-1 / F-1242-2 — 129th ask, restart pid 35584** · 🔺 F-1193-3 · 🔺 gold-per-token · 🔺 F-1209-3 · 🔺 TOWN ZOOM clamps · 🔺 F-1185-1 · 🔺 F-1208-3 · 🔺 F-1204-1 · 🔺 F-1141-3+F-1164-1 · 🔻 F-1182-2 `brew upgrade codex` (112th) · plus all carried. ⓘ **Unchanged attended items:** `specs/agent-play/README.md:2` still reads STATUS: DRAFT. F-1260-3's numbering collision unrepaired. 💡 **THE THROUGH-LINE.** *s1291 found a guard's green is its weakest evidence · s1292 that a list inherited as a set is a claim about every member · s1293 that a §F is a hypothesis whose answer often sits inside its own citation · s1294 that "it's probably load" is a hypothesis wearing a verdict's clothes.* **Mine is that A VERIFICATION IS ONLY AS GOOD AS THE REFERENCE IT IS TAKEN AGAINST, AND `HEAD` IS NOT A FIXED REFERENCE.** s1294 did everything right — checked out, gated, reverted, confirmed clean — and reached a false conclusion, because the thing it measured *against* had moved underneath it. ⚡ **No amount of care at the `git status` layer could have caught this; only a different instrument could.** And the instrument was not clever: it was a `throw` in my own harness comparing an expected blob to an observed one, which fired within seconds of starting. **When a check keeps returning the answer you expect, ask what it is denominated against — and prefer a probe that names an absolute value (a hash) over one that reports a relationship (`clean`, `ahead`, `no diff`), because a relationship silently re-bases when either end moves.**
