tasks/BACKLOG.md:306:🟢 **F-1585-1 (s1585 2026-08-09, MEASURED THIS FIRE — THE GZ-01 STANDING SWEEP RETURNS ZERO BACKFILLS OWED, AND ITS PRESCRIBED ONE-COMMAND CHECK PRODUCES A 23% FALSE-ALARM RATE ON A HEALTHY WINDOW. NO CORRECTIVE AUTHORED AND NONE WANTED — THE LAW ALREADY FORBIDS THE MECHANISM THIS WOULD TEMPT).** ✓ **SWEEP RUN, first since F-1546-1 made it standing:** `--first-parent main --since=2026-08-06`, **31 `src/`-touching commits · 24 already in `gazette-queue.md` · 7 absent · all 7 correctly absent.** Full evidence + per-commit dismissals: `artifacts/s1585-gz01-backfill-sweep.md`. **The pipeline is HEALTHY; this is a sweep returning the answer a sweep exists to be able to return.** ⚠️ **METHOD CORRECTION MADE MID-SWEEP, AND IT IS THE REUSABLE HALF:** the first pass used `git show --pretty=format: --name-only`, which is **blind to merge commits** — it reported `review[NONE]` for `c41ba89de` while hiding `reviews/milk-twin-sockets.md` **and 340 new src lines (`AtomicSocket.ts`, `DeepwaterSocket.ts`)**, and did not surface `d66bdbe35`, `f315ecd2b` or `716f3e298` at all. **Four of the seven absent commits — the entire interesting cluster — were invisible or mis-read**, so a sweep trusting it would have reported "nothing to see" for the wrong reason and been right by accident. ➡️ **Any future sweep MUST pass `--diff-merges=first-parent`.** 🔍 **NO TWO OF THE SEVEN WERE DISMISSIBLE BY THE SAME EVIDENCE, which is the finding:** (1–4) the **era-socket cluster** (E4 motor, E5 deepwater, E6 atomic, E9 arsenal+canal) carries review files and real new src, and is refuted as player-visible by **product code, not opinion** — the `SUPPORTED_CONTRACTS` allowlist in `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts` admits **twelve contracts, E1(5)+E2(4)+E3(3), nothing above E3**, above a comment stating *"E5/E6 stay out DESPITE their era sockets now running headlessly … Admission was attempted and MEASURED, and the measurement refused it"*. **The sockets exist; the epochs are not admitted