tasks/BACKLOG.md:654:🔺 **F-PG-2 (2026-08-04, MEASURED — `LANDMARK_EMISSIVE` WAS DEAD CODE, SO THREE ALREADY-MERGED BEAUTY UPGRADES ON THREE OTHER MAPS HAD SILENTLY REVERTED THEMSELVES. CURED ON TWO BRANCHES AT ONCE; THEY WILL COLLIDE.)** `Terrain3dClaimPilot.ts` applied the per-contract landmark paint and then, four lines later, called `keepLandmarkPaintReadable(model)` again with **no** argument — re-applying `DEFAULT_LANDMARK_PAINT` (`#ffffff`, intensity 3) over the top. Dead: **the Claim's U3 1.45**, **e1-baron's U2 four-body grade** (emissive half; the diffuse tint survived), **`DRY_GULCH_SPRING_EMISSIVE` 2.1**. ⚠️ **Nothing could have told anyone, because `dataset.terrain3dPilotLandmarkEmissive` is written straight from the lookup — it publishes the DECLARATION, not the material.** Proven by pixels, not by reading: registering 1.45 moved the manifold crop **0.1 luma** (noise); deleting the duplicate moved it **92.7 → 82.4, stddev 42.1 → 32.1** — blown self-lit highlights collapsing into modelled form. `landmark-brightness.spec.ts` green both projects after. Root cause per the parallel shift: `10586b90` (the baron drain) kept both the new per-contract block and the single-line call it replaced. 🚨 **`beauty2/e2-hill-mine` found the identical bug the same day (its F-BHM-1) and deleted the same line in `bc14d54c`, additionally publishing the MEASURED per-mount `emissiveIntensity` in `terrain3dPilotLandmarkMaterials[]`. Main still carries the duplicate as of `7c833197`, so whichever branch drains second CONFLICTS on this hunk. RESOLUTION: keep the deletion, prefer hill-mine's measured-value publication.** GATE: drain both branches, then one probe confirming the Claim, the Baron and Dry Gulch render at their reviewed intensities.
