tasks/BACKLOG.md:1692:🟠 **F-1176-1 (s1176, MEASURED, corrective AUTHORED + QUEUED) — THE EIGHT-WINDS BLOCKER IS A CLASS OF 26 CELLS ACROSS TWO SHEETS, NOT THE 9 THE RUNNER COULD SEE — AND THE SHEET ITS SCOPE MISSED IS THE WORSE ONE.** Slice 1 (`lane-c-eight-winds-wiring-hero`) **STOPPED LAWFULLY** at `anim-pass-reextract.mjs --verify-downscale`, and correctly so — but **not where s1175 predicted.** All three scope-1 premises **HELD** (F-1175-1 and F-1175-2 both confirmed in the lane, the second reproducing its predicted skip message verbatim), so the stop came *past* them. ✓ **THE CLASS WAS MEASURED THREE INDEPENDENT WAYS, ALL AGREEING EXACTLY:** (1) **git provenance** — is a shipped cell's last-touching commit newer than its master's? → **26 = 17 `char-baron-sheet-walk8` + 9 `char-hero-sheet-walk8`**, and this method **PREDICTED baron=17 before a single pixel was compared**; (2) **the pixel control per sheet** — hero `23 byte-identical / 9 mismatched` (reproducing the runner's numbers *and filenames* exactly), baron `15 / **17**` (confirming the prediction); (3) **the pixel control over the WHOLE TREE** — `389 byte-identical, **26 mismatched**, 0 with no shipped copy (of 415 masters)`. 9+17=26 ⇒ **no third sheet exists; the class is closed.** 🔑 **Read the whole-tree line twice: 389 of 415 cells reproduce byte-identically, so the resize is PROVEN CORRECT and every failure is a contaminated reference set.** **PROVENANCE ACCOUNTS FOR ALL 26:** `21dc8739` *"fix-walk-cutout-pockets"* (07-13) changed **80** shipped cells and **ZERO** masters; `04732223` *"town-cast-metrology"* (07-12) changed **3** and **ZERO**. ⚠️ **SECOND, SEPARATE HAZARD — LATENT, NOT LIVE, AND STATED AT ITS REAL SEVERITY:** because those masters lack the mends, a flagless global `optimize-assets.mjs` would **silently REVERT** them (it reads the master, downscales, overwrites the shipped cell — `:92-112`), on the hero (what a player watches all run) and the baron. ✓ **Verified ARMED BUT NOT AUTOMATIC: that script has NO automated caller** — not in `package.json`, not in any script or CI; it is a manual step and `anim-pass-reextract.mjs` exists precisely to avoid it. **Nothing is broken in today's build.** ⛔ **No fire rewrites those 26 masters** — that is 26 cells of shipped-quality art and an attended/owner data call; the corrective's scope 1 is a measure-and-report STOP that hands that session its evidence, and its firewall forbids touching a pixel. Review `reviews/eight-winds-wiring-hero.md`; run report merged at `tasks/runs/20260728-172245-…`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1693:🟠 **F-1176-2 (s1176) — THE CONTROL THAT STOPPED THE RUN CAN NEVER PASS ON THOSE TWO SHEETS, AND WOULD HAVE BLOCKED THE NEXT RUNG HARDER.** `--verify-downscale` (`anim-pass-reextract.mjs:102-118`) re-derives shipped cells from masters and byte-compares, to prove *its resize matches `optimize-assets.mjs`'s*. **That claim is true and now strongly evidenced (389/415).** The defect is its **reference set**: its own comment says it checks *"untouched shipped cells"*, but **"untouched" is an assumption the code never checks and cannot check** — there is no exclusion list, no provenance test, just `process.exit(bad ? 1 : 0)`. So **any sheet carrying even one deliberate post-extraction mend is a permanent red**, for a reason unrelated to the claim under test. ➡️ **This sat on the ladder's critical path:** the **baron** is one of the five non-hero `walk8` slots the next rung must bind and carries **17** contaminated cells — nearly double the hero's — so that rung was going to hit the same wall, harder, and so would every future animation mend on either sheet. **CORRECTIVE `tasks/lane-c-eight-winds-master-convention.md` AUTHORED + QUEUED → lane-c** (leaf `eight-winds-master-convention` same commit; `drain-block-check --queue` ✅ CLEAR before the `cp`; `goal-tracker` **2/2** before both `goals.json` commits): a tracked `master-divergent` manifest + three bucket counts (`byte-identical` / `unexplained` / `master-divergent by design`), exit 0 only when `unexplained == 0`, **and the control keeps all its teeth** — an unlisted mismatch, a **stale exclusion** that now reproduces cleanly, or a manifest entry naming a missing file each still exit 1. Scope 3 mutates the **SUBJECT** (an unlisted cell, a removed entry, a bogus entry), never the guard script. **Zero pixels change.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1701:🔻 **F-1175-1 (s1175) — THE WIRING SPEC'S `src/` RECOMMENDATION IS AIMED AT THE WRONG MAP, AND IT WOULD HAVE FAILED EXACTLY THE SLOTS THAT NEED IT MOST.** `reviews/eight-winds-wiring-spec.md` §3.1 states that `SpriteAnimator.ts:843` *"already skips an alias when an explicit direction exists but only for `charHero`"* and offers, as *"the better change and the only `src/` line this surface needs"*, widening that guard to *"any slot with an explicit direction of this name"*. **I read the line instead of the sentence.** It is `if (slotId === assetSlots.charHero && slot?.rotations?.directions?.[targetDirection]) continue;` — the condition tests **`slot.rotations.directions`**, a *different contract surface* from the `walk8` block's own `directions` map that the wiring populates (`expandWalkSheetSources:998` overlays the latter; the alias loop at `:841` overwrites it afterwards). ✓ **Then I measured the data, and the two halves disagree in the load-bearing direction:** `char.hero` carries **all eight** `rotations.directions` keys, so its aliases are **already inert** — that is *why* slice 1 needs no `src/` — but `char.bandit_base`, `char.bandit_thief`, `char.baron` and `char.prospector_agent` carry an **EMPTY** `rotations.directions`, so **widening the slot test changes nothing for them**; they would still be overwritten to due-east/due-west. `char.claim_jumper` has `se`/`ne` but **no `sw`/`nw`** — half-covered. ➡️ **The spec's PRIMARY option — emptying the `aliases` map — is the one that actually works**, and `char.bandit_base` is the fallback art for **ten** slots, so it is the highest-reach sheet in the program. **Left undecided on purpose:** slice 1 leaves every `aliases` map untouched and instead makes the hero's inertness *executable* (a test that goes red the day someone deletes `char.hero`'s `rotations.directions`). 🔁 *Reusable shape: **a spec's recommendation is an untested second hypothesis, and a citation is not a conclusion** — the spec cited the right line number and drew the wrong inference from it; opening the file cost two minutes and moved the fix from "one line in `src/`" to "a data change the master must not make yet".*
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1806:🔑 **F-1156-3 (s1156 — ⚠️ SUPERSEDED AS A WORK ITEM by F-1158-1 above; the mechanism was right, the count and the payoff were not) — F-1150-2 RE-MEASURED BEFORE AUTHORING, AND THE RE-MEASUREMENT BOTH REFUTED IT AS A CONSOLIDATION TASK *AND* EXPLAINED WHY F-1152-1 TOOK FIVE FIRES TO SEE.** s1155 named F-1150-2 "the one substantial fire-authorable item left, author it when lanes are quiet". Lanes were quiet this fire, so I measured it instead of queueing it. **It is not 22 duplicates — it is 23 files containing 18 DISTINCT helper bodies**, largest identical group **3 files**, across **10 signatures with incompatible return types** (`void`, `HpEntry`, `HpEntry & {cost}`, `BuildEntry`, `BuildableEntry`, `number`, plus `rotated`/`upgradeTo` params and one taking a `ShotAction`). ➡️ **There is no shared helper to extract.** Forcing 18 behaviours through one signature is the **Vocabulary Stretch (Mistake #14)** in its exact shape, and an options-bag helper would be worse than the duplication. **DO NOT AUTHOR the consolidation** — the finding's premise ("drifting signatures" implying copy-paste) does not survive measurement. 🔑 **AND THE MEASUREMENT PAID FOR ITSELF ELSEWHERE: 17 of the 23 helpers poll `ghostValid` before confirming, and the 6 that do NOT are `f1148-1-trajectory-probe`, `m2-04-gold-stealing`, `054-baron-epic`, `m2-01-build-menu`, `polish-02-rivalry-stats`, `m2-06-arsenal-blast-charge` — i.e. the two specs where the F-1152-1 flake was ever observed are BOTH in the unguarded six.** ✓ **Mechanism verified at source:** `updateActionActorPosition()` runs every fixed tick (`Game.ts:2248`, immediately after `simTick += 1`), so `expect.poll(() => ghostValid).toBe(true)` simply **blocks until the next tick refreshes the stale position** — it is, mechanically, an ad-hoc workaround for F-1152-1 that 17 specs grew independently. ➡️ **That is why the bug looked rare: it was masked in 74% of the specs that could have shown it.** ⚠️ **Consequence now that F-1153-1 has landed: those 17 polls are REDUNDANT** — `teleport()` is synchronous again. Removing them is a real e2e-hygiene slice with a measurable payoff (suite wall-time), but it is a 17-file change and should wait until the cure has held across a few fires. **Recorded, deliberately not authored.**
