tasks/BACKLOG.md:2870:- 🔬 **F-1068-3 SOLVED — the engine locked the card CORRECTLY and the fixture was under-seeded.** `e1-baron`'s rule is `science-complete+2-secured` (`src/meta/ContractUnlock.ts:48-54`), requiring science complete **and** `securedContracts.size >= 2` — *two distinct secured contract ids*. The fixture seeded exactly one (`the-claim`), so `data-contract-locked="true"` was the right answer. Seeding `e1-dry-gulch` as the second makes the fixture model a player who has genuinely earned the whole E1 board — **a precondition repair, not a bent expectation**: the unlock rule is untouched and the neighbouring rungs stay coherent (`e1-dry-gulch` = `wave10OnClaim`, `e1-twin-banks` = `firstSecuredClaim`, `e1-night-shift` = `science≥3`).
tasks/BACKLOG.md:2976:✅ **F-1081-3 SHIPPED — rf-26 DRAINED s1088, merged as `dc483d74927bcdd694c9aeb4c61144ecd225acb5`, review `reviews/rf-26.md`, goal leaf `rf-26-entry-damage-net` flipped `merged` in the drain commit.** The ladder tune now has a net: `scripts/entry-damage-table.test.mjs`, 6 assertions importing the REAL `Balance.waves.entryDamageScale`, wired into `test:node-guards` (43 → **49 tests, 49 pass**, the new 6 visible ⇒ it is genuinely invoked by the lane, not merely added). Gates: tsc 0 · build 0 (1934 modules) · guard 6/6 · node-guards `node --test` phase 49/49 **twice** · serial `--test-concurrency=1` 49/49 rc 0. **No playwright and that is a ruling, not an omission** — `src/game/Balance.ts` ends blob-identical to main (`0d918dc1`) and the diff is one `scripts/` file plus one `package.json` line, so the slice has **zero runtime surface**. 🔬 **THREE mutation controls re-run BY HAND (the runner's two, plus one of mine on the sign-inversion assertion, which was otherwise a green nobody had watched fail)** — all three reddened their intended assertion, all reverted, empty `git diff -- src/game/Balance.ts`. ⭐ **AND THE CONTROL TAUGHT SOMETHING WORTH KEEPING: under a 12-entry table, `nightShift[12]` is STILL `undefined`, so F-1081-3's own literal ask ("wave 3 reduced, wave 12 not") stayed GREEN while the table was silently resized — only the BOUNDARY assertion s1087 added on top of the finding caught it. The net is stronger than the finding that ordered it, and now there is a measurement saying so.** ⚠️ **RESIDUAL, re-homed rather than left implied: the net does NOT cover the `spawnAt` parameter-reordering risk** (3 of 4 named risks covered, plus 2 the finding never asked for) — that half is **blocked on F-1077-3**, which is now the highest-value fire-authorable item on the board precisely because findings queue behind it. Original authoring note: 🟢 **F-1081-3 AUTHORED s1087 as `tasks/lane-entry-damage-net.md` (goal leaf `rf-26-entry-damage-net`, registered same commit), QUEUED TO LANE-A — THE LADDER TUNE FINALLY GETS A NET.** Authored because **F-1086-1 proved the silent-rot class is real and live this week**: the Mistake-#10 plain-boot test was found deterministically red on main, recorded as PASSING at ship, and listed nowhere — it rotted because nothing was watching. `Balance.waves.entryDamageScale` is in exactly that position today. ✓ **PREMISES RE-VERIFIED s1087 by reading the code, not the finding:** the table is `src/game/Balance.ts:5-8`, exposed at `:89`, and is **11 entries (indices 0–10)** — `'e1-night-shift'` and `'e1-baron'` both `[0.2 ×7, 0.5 ×4]`; the lookup is a **direct array index on the wave number** (`WaveSystem.ts:513-515`), applied as `(options.contactDamageScale ?? 1) * entryDamageScale` (`:521-523`), with `applyEntryDamageScale` the **9th positional parameter** (`:487`) and exactly one opt-out call site (`:365`). So F-1081-3's asked-for assertions resolve to **wave 3 → 0.2 (reduced)** and **wave 12 → `undefined` (unscaled)** — ✓ both confirmed against the real table. **THREE RULINGS DECIDED BY MEASUREMENT rather than left to the runner, because two attractive approaches are dead ends I actually tested:** **(1)** the guard imports the **real `Balance.ts`** — ✓ **PROVED headlessly importable** (it only imports `three`); a guard that re-states its own numbers tests nothing. **(2) `spawnAt` is NOT tested and NO `src/` debug bridge may be added to reach it** — ✗ `WaveSystem.ts` **fails to import**: *"TypeScript parameter property is not supported in strip-only mode"*; ✗ there is **no wave/enemy test global anywhere in `e2e/`** (verified), so a browser-side test would mean inventing one — scope invention (§7.3) under a firewall that has lawfully STOPPED two prior rounds (F-1082-1); ✗ and the rig is **barred by F-1081-3 itself** until F-1077-3 is fixed. **(3)** assert the **BOUNDARY** (wave 10 defined, wave 11 `undefined`), not merely F-1081-3's two interior samples, which would both survive an off-by-one. ⚠️ **THE LIMIT IS STATED IN THE MASTER AND IS A REPORTING DUTY, NOT BURIED: this net does NOT cover the `spawnAt` parameter-reordering risk** F-1081-3 names — it covers **3 of the 4** (table dropped · contract id mistyped/renamed · values regressed) **plus two the finding did not ask for** (the boundary, and a sign inversion where an entry `> 1` would *increase* early damage — silent today). The master requires the runner to state that gap in its own report so the drain cannot over-claim it. **Two mandatory mutation controls** (wave-3 `0.2→1`; a 12th entry appended) each proven RED then reverted, with an **empty `git diff -- src/game/Balance.ts`** as the proof. **LANE SAFETY ✓ PROVED THIS FIRE:** `lane/m3` reads 1 ahead (`f231b073`) but that is rf-23, **content-merged as `7be9ce7b…`** (same `taskFile`, goal leaf merged), and `git diff main lane/m3 -- src/ e2e/ functions/` shows **zero `src/` difference** and the branch only *behind* ⇒ the reset is **loss-free**.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:3062:🟡 **F-1081-1 — A LANE REPORT'S OWN RED-CLASSIFICATION WAS HALF-CHECKED, AND IT SKIPPED THE TWO SUITES THAT EXERCISE THE CODE IT CHANGED.** `reviews/e1-ladder-tune.md` (Codex, on-branch) stated "All 8 failures are the same four Night Shift lighting/suspend failures on desktop and mobile; **the four desktop failures** reproduce unchanged on clean base" — it fingerprinted **desktop only** while asserting a verdict over all 8. The claim happened to be true (s1081 confirmed all 8 identical on clean main across both projects by cp-revert), but it was **luck, not evidence**. More consequentially, its battery covered only Night Shift + Baron and **never ran `m1-03-wave-pressure` or `m2-03-wave-scheduler`** — the two suites that exercise `spawnAt`, the exact function it modified. Both carry pre-existing reds (`m2-03:126 wave>=14 got 10`; `m1-03:31` grace `enemiesAlive` ≠ 0), so the first drain battery to include them surfaces 4 new-looking failures on a spawn-path change — a textbook setup for blaming a correct slice. ➡️ **Standing lesson for authoring: a task's self-check must name the suites that cover the FUNCTION it edits, not just the FEATURE it targets.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:3064:🟡 **F-1081-2 — TWO MORE TESTS JOIN THE LOAD-FLAKY SET.** `e2e/e1-night-shift.spec.ts:413` ("lantern coverage is necessary for threat visibility") and `e2e/e1-baron.spec.ts:343` ("contract board requires science plus two secured claims…") each failed in **exactly one of four s1081 batteries**, with the graft held constant: 413 failed at 5-spec load and passed at 2-spec load; 343 did the reverse. A moving failure under a fixed cause is flake, not regression (the F-1078-2 / gate-battery-contention class). 413's failing read was `spriteLuminance >= 0.35, got 0.219 / 0.275` — a luminance sample, so heavy parallel GPU load is the plausible mechanism. ➡️ Worth a stabilisation rung (isolate or single-worker these two); **no corrective queued**, and until then a drain that trips either should re-run it isolated before believing it.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:3066:✅ **CLOSED s1088 — the net shipped as rf-26, `dc483d74927bcdd694c9aeb4c61144ecd225acb5` (see the SHIPPED line above; residual `spawnAt` risk re-homed onto F-1077-3).** 🟡 **F-1081-3 — THE E1 LADDER TUNE HAS NO REGRESSION NET (owner-visible risk, small).** `Balance.waves.entryDamageScale` + `applyEntryDamageScale` shipped in `eb7278ac` with **no spec asserting any of it**. The only proof the opening is now walkable is a manual `rehearsal/segments/e1-depth-play.mjs` run (Night Shift died wave 9→11, Baron 3→16). So: reorder `spawnAt`'s parameters, mistype a contract id, or drop the table and **nothing goes red** — the two named contracts would quietly return to killing a new player in the first minutes, which is precisely the release-blocking symptom this slice existed to fix. s1081 merged it anyway because the wiring was verified by reading all six `spawnAt` call sites (only the debug `spawnStressEnemies` opts out) and the table indices check out 1-based. ➡️ **Owed: a cheap spec asserting a wave-3 spawn on `e1-night-shift` carries a reduced `contactDamageScale` and a wave-12 spawn does not.** Fire-authorable (no design fork, no canon). Note it should NOT be built on the rig until F-1077-3 is fixed — that harness still defaults its own port and can measure a foreign tree.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:3115:🟢 **F-1102-1 — F-1101-2 IS ROOT-CAUSED AND QUEUED AS `078-focus-and-ledger-reverts` (lane-c). s1101 guessed "same family ⇒ likely one cause, not three"; the truth is THREE REVERTED FIXES ACROSS TWO COMMITS, and that guess would have sent a fixer hunting one imaginary shared cause.** ✓ VERIFIED s1102 by reading each diff, **with no test run at all** — s1101 left a whole-suite baseline running detached (pid 80822) and any control would have contaminated it (its own §D admits exactly that self-contamination). `e2e/078-ux-hygiene.spec.ts` has **one** commit in its life (`cd76c7f0`, 2026-07-10) and never moved again; the product moved on 2026-07-11 and took three fixes down with it. **(1) `:151`** — `93632a94` (audio MU-02 wave 1) collapsed `TownScene.openBoard`'s two-query `??` into ONE grouped `querySelector`, which returns first-in-**document-order** across the whole group, so the header's `data-contract-close` beats every contract card and Launch is never focused; that hunk deleted **verbatim the entire product change of `cd76c7f0`**, the commit that created this spec. **(2) `:130`** — `9b567437` (en-03 epoch pages) deleted `currentRestoreFocus`, the close-time focus restore, the `Tab` branch and `trapLedgerFocus()` from `src/encyclopedia/reader.ts` (−34 lines), reverting `acf1c476`. **(3) `:111`** — **the same commit `9b567437`** reverted `discoverLedgerEntry` from the unfiltered `readStoredDiscoveryValues` back to the filtering `readStoredDiscovered`, so an unknown id is dropped on read and the write-back yields `['baron']` instead of `['future-ledger-id','baron']` — undoing `e1f243f4`. **All three reproduce at BOTH `--workers=8` and `--workers=4`, so they are NOT F-1101-1 contention artefacts**; `:111` failed in 1.5 s in both runs. The master carries **RULING 3** (KEEP the newer unconditional `stopPropagation()` at `reader.ts:334` — it post-dates `acf1c476` and has a deliberate multiplayer rationale, so a literal revert-of-the-revert would regress multiplayer input) and **RULING 6** (the `aria-modal`/`inert` alternative to a JS focus trap is a product decision → **OWNER-GATED, flagged not implemented**).
tasks/BACKLOG.md:3132:🟠 **F-1107-1 — THE CALIBRATION VOIDED ITSELF ON A 17.88% "DRIFT" THAT WAS ONE FLAKY TEST, NOT AN UNSTABLE BOX — SO ITS OWN REMEDY ("re-run on a stable box") WOULD BE VOIDED AGAIN. F-1101-1 REMAINS OPEN.** ✓ VERIFIED s1107 by re-deriving p95 from the report's published duration table; the parse reproduces its author's own figures (**17.9s / 14.7s**) exactly, so it is validated against the thing it audits. `lane-calibrate-suite-workers` ran its full `1,2,4,8,1` sequence and then **STOPped lawfully under its own Ruling 5**: the two `workers=1` controls disagreed at p95 by 17.88% against a predeclared 15% ceiling, so **no worker count was pinned and no guard shipped** — `playwright.config.ts` is untouched and the whole-suite gate still poisons itself. **But the drift is not box instability: 40 of the 43 tests reproduce within ±0.5s across the two controls.** The single mover is **`055-baron-kill-stop.spec.ts:121` at −9.8s**, which was w1's **lone red** *and* its **largest duration (21.6s)**, going green at 11.8s in the repeat. Since **p95 nearest-rank at n=43 reads the 3rd-largest value**, greening that one test is by itself sufficient to walk p95 from 17.9s → 14.7s. That is the entire "drift". ➡️ **TWO CONSEQUENCES FOR THE RE-RUN, both cheap:** (1) **the instrument's greenness was established from ONE banked w4 log** — the subset was frozen as "fully green" precisely so failures could not confound the duration signal, and a failure confounded it exactly as feared; **s1104(D)'s standing law — *a control run ONCE is a coin toss* — applies to instrument SELECTION, not just to fingerprinting**, so re-derive the subset from repeated runs or drop `055:121`; (2) **compute the drift control over green tests only**, because at n=43 the metric is dominated by its top 3 samples by construction. The provisional **`workers=2`** result (the only candidate with inflation ≤1.25, max ≤25s, zero reds) stands **unpromoted but uncontradicted**. ⚠️ **RED HERRING, recorded so the next fire does not chase it:** the repeat's accepted quiescence samples were `{ 3.14 25.14 21.29 }` vs the first w1's `{ 2.20 2.51 3.43 }` — a ~**8× higher 5-minute load**, because the gate only ever tested the **1-minute** figure, which recovers in ~2 min while the 5/15-min averages stay elevated long after the w8 saturation. It looks like the culprit and **is not**: despite that 8× gap, 40 of 43 tests still landed within ±0.5s. Worth tightening the gate regardless. Landed report-only (pure-add, 5 raw logs + `reviews/calib-suite-workers.md`, 1354 insertions / zero deletions, classified against merge-base `91d511e6`); **no battery run or owed — no `src`/`e2e`/`scripts`/config file changed.** Goal leaf `calibrate-suite-workers` → **`diagnosed`**, deliberately NOT `merged`, so no future fire reads F-1101-1 as closed.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:3134:🟠 **F-1107-2 — `055-baron-kill-stop.spec.ts:121` IS A GENUINE FLAKE, IT IS **NOT** THE rf-37 CLASS, AND IT IS LOAD-*IN*DEPENDENT.** ✓ VERIFIED s1107 by reading the test at source. It uses `expect.poll` throughout and **never holds-then-releases a key before polling for an arrival**, so the `rf-37` (`lane-approach-steer-to-arrival`) cure does not apply and **it must not be added to that master's 9-site list** — adding it would blunt a master whose whole value is that its 9 sites share one measured shape. Its reds are not contention artefacts either: it **failed under `w1`, the quietest condition in the entire sequence**, and passed at w2, w4 and the w1 repeat. Mechanism undiagnosed; likeliest suspects are its fixed **8s/5s poll budgets** around the ceremony transition (`test.setTimeout(45_000)`, ceremony-active and `victory-sting` polls at 8s). **OWED as its own small investigation** — and note it is currently *inside* F-1101-1's frozen calibration subset, which is how it voided the experiment above.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:3166:🟢 **F-1107-2 DOWNGRADED s1114 — `055-baron-kill-stop.spec.ts:121` DID **NOT** REPRODUCE, 8/8, AND ITS FOUNDING PREMISE ("load-INdependent") NOW LOOKS LIKE THE CONTENTION IT WAS DEFINED AGAINST.** ✓ VERIFIED by execution on a quiet box (loadavg 1.93 → 2.6), every run at `--workers=1`, the owed investigation finally taken. **Isolated (`:121` alone): 5/5 PASS at 13–14s** against a `test.setTimeout(45_000)` budget — ~31s of headroom, not a test scraping its ceiling. **Whole file (4 tests, so `:121` runs with its siblings' accumulated browser state): 3/3 PASS at 33.7 / 34.4 / 34.1s.** F-1107-2 was founded on a single red measured at `w1` during s1107's 43-test calibration sequence, and reasoned *"it failed under w1, the quietest condition in the entire sequence, therefore it is not a contention artefact."* **That inference does not survive F-1113-4**, which showed a guard the slice never touched going red on contention alone: `--workers=1` bounds *playwright's own* parallelism, it does not make the box quiet, and a long battery is not a quiet condition merely because it is serial. ⚖️ **HONEST STATISTICAL LIMIT, stated rather than buried: 8/8 green does not close it.** At F-1107-2's own implied in-battery rate (~1 in 4), eight clean runs would occur by luck ~10% of the time. So this is a **downgrade from "genuine load-independent flake, mechanism undiagnosed" to "does not reproduce in isolation or in-file on a quiet box"** — not a closure. ✍️ **AUTHORED s1114 — `tasks/lane-cw-02-wrecker-target-premise.md` (goal leaf `cw-02-wrecker-target-premise`), QUEUED SAME FIRE to lane-a**, byte-identical to the committed master (sha256 `46497ff9…`), `^CODEX:` ✓ verified at **column 0 on line 9** of the *queued copy* (F-1088-4). Closes F-1114-3, the last red of the F-1109-1 → F-1112-1 chain. **The evidence chain is this fire's own measurements, not an inheritance.** ⚠️ **The master's most important content is what it FORBIDS, because two hypotheses are already dead and re-running them would burn the run:** raising `advanceSim` is a firewall violation (5× changed nothing) and "the engine mis-targets" is answered at source (`Enemy.ts:1040-1075`, `nearestBuilding`). **SCOPE 1 IS A MANDATORY MEASUREMENT THAT GATES THE FIX** — print every `build.hp` entry's world position and its distance to the west gate `(-46, 38)` — then branch: **(2a)** a lantern *is* nearer ⇒ the premise is stale, rewrite the assertion to express its **intent** (*the structure nearest the west gate takes exactly one hit*, derived at runtime, never named by index), re-deciding `:135` in the same edit since the same event falsifies it; **(2b)** no lantern is nearer ⇒ `nearestBuilding` picks a farther target, which is a real engine bug and a **lawful STOP to the owner's desk with zero `src/` changes**. 🛡️ **The sharpest clause is anti-cargo-cult, and it is stated as such: re-pointing the assertion at whatever happened to get hit is explicitly forbidden — that is writing the guard from the answer sheet, it would go green while proving nothing, and being unable to express the intent is itself a VALID STOP.** Baseline banked for the whole family at `--workers=1`: **3 passed / 1 failed (45.9s)**. LANE-SAFETY pre-proved s1114: `main..lane/m3` is the single commit this fire drained itself (`70ce6e50`), its two-dot `src/`+`e2e/` diff vs main is **EMPTY**, worktree clean, queue empty ⇒ safe dupe, the reset loses nothing.
