tasks/BACKLOG.md:3625:- ✅ CLOSED s1499 — **F-1462-1 — ER-02 SHIPPED WITHOUT EITHER RULING: the two owner questions were DISSOLVED, NOT ANSWERED, by taking the HEADLESS door.** The rehearsal merged `bb969fb3` (`reviews/standing-orders-rehearsal-e2.md`, 8 metered runs). Both premises below are TRUE **and both are facts about the BROWSER harness only** — ✓ RE-VERIFIED AT THE DRAIN by reading the merged review’s own evidence, not by trusting it: **(1) board access** — the unlock chain is real, but `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts` contains no unlock/board/lock reference at all, so the shift booted the two DEEPEST cards in the chain directly across 38 run directories with no `?debug` era-seed and no honesty liberty; **(2) who the rider is** — the 7-minute blocking wait is `rehearsal/r2-loop.mjs:53`’s, not the protocol’s, and the whole eight-run card re-runs end to end in a TIMED 31 s (1.4 s per 14-wave run) against 300–600 s per contract for the E1 browser rounds. ⭐ **THE REUSABLE PART: a slice can be blocked by a property of the INSTRUMENT its author assumed, not of the work.** F-1462-1 was correct, careful, and re-derived across several fires — and it was answering *how do we ride the browser*, a question ER-02 never had to ask. Before carrying a two-ruling block to the desk, check whether a second shipped door makes the block vacuous (**precedent: a blocker true of one transport is vacuous in another**). ⓘ The recommendation it made — scope to hill-mine + pressure-garden, run ATTENDED — was **not** what shipped, and the trestle/incline pair it called unreachable is exactly what got played. **RETAINED VERBATIM BELOW (superseded, not deleted):** 🟡 **F-1462-1 — ER-02 IS NOW UNBLOCKED ON EVERY GATE ANYONE WROTE DOWN, AND IS STILL NOT AUTHORABLE: it needs two owner rulings first (board ACCESS, and WHO THE RIDER IS).** With F-1460-1 closed above, s1462 re-checked ER-02’s stated dependency — `specs/e2-readiness/README.md:10` *"Depends: ER-01 drivers + ER-00 determinism"* — and **both conjuncts are satisfied**: ER-00 determinism via `f1405-1` `eaefdb24` + twin-banks `f1412-1` `2c22b2ab` + baron `f1413-1`, and ER-01 (which `:9` scopes to the **E2** census only, NOT the E3–E10 ladder gated on F-1461-6) merged at `96d40988`. The census is **CURRENT, not stale** — `dcf02430` inside merge `24c6600f` rewrote it, so main reads **2 AGENT-READY / 2 DATA-GAP / 0 BROKEN** (`e2-pressure-garden`, `e2-incline` ready; `e2-hill-mine`, `e2-trestle` cross GR-SIM’s wave-14 ceiling without emitting `secured`/`died`). No duplicate master exists, all six queues are empty, and no open `GATE:` line names ER-02. ⚠️ **BUT THE SLICE CANNOT STATE A RUNNABLE SCOPE, AND BOTH REASONS ARE DESIGN FORKS, SO §2E’S HARD LIMIT FORBIDS A FIRE AUTHORING IT.** **(1) BOARD ACCESS.** The E2 board is a serial unlock chain — `assets/contracts/epoch-2-steamworks/contracts.json` gates `e2-trestle` on `secured:e2-hill-mine`, `e2-pressure-garden` on `secured:e2-trestle`, `e2-incline` on `secured:e2-pressure-garden`, and the era itself on `epochMegaprojectComplete` (Dynamo Hall, 8 banked science) — **so the two AGENT-READY contracts are the two DEEPEST in it**, and the harness hard-fails on a locked card (`rehearsal/r2-loop.mjs:223`). The only bypass is `?debug` era-seeding (`src/meta/DebugEraSeed.ts:9`), which the honest-play gate explicitly forbids (`rehearsal/r2-loop.mjs:4-6`). **(2) WHO THE RIDER IS.** The harness blocks up to **7 minutes per call** (`SO2_RIDER_WAIT` 420_000, `r2-loop.mjs:53`) waiting for an `orders-<seq>.json` that **a model in another process** must write; both E1 rounds were attended Opus sessions for exactly that reason, and round 2 measured that rider latency SETS the call count (*"A FASTER RIDER IS A MORE EXPENSIVE RIDER"*). **A Codex lane task cannot be the rider** — making it one changes what the rehearsal proves, which is a premise change, not a detail. 💡 **RECOMMENDATION (one word each): (a)** scope ER-02 to `e2-hill-mine` + `e2-pressure-garden`, era-seed