tasks/BACKLOG.md:3643:- ⛔ **F-1474-1 (s1474, AUTHORED → RAN AND STOPPED s1475; SUPERSEDED BY F-1475-1 BELOW — the socket ANALYSIS held, the ACCEPTANCE PATH did not) — E3 ERA-SOCKET #6: THE FAIR WHEEL. The cheapest socket in the class, because the finding that describes it went STALE IN OUR FAVOUR.** `tasks/lane-e3-fairground-socket.md` → lane-a (leaf `e3-fairground-socket`), narrows **F-ER01-E3-4**. 🔑 **The finding says "GR-SIM has neither system" — measured s1474 on main, that is no longer true, and only ONE consumer is missing.** `twist.powerGrid` is already socketed at `HeadlessContractSim.ts:245` and `twist.dayNightCycle` at `:256`, both landed by this leaf’s own predecessors (`3ac90dd8`, `2256ee58`); the sole gap is `src/entities/FerrisWheel.ts`, which is browser-only. ⭐ **And `e3-fairground` has NO baron** (`twist` = `secureWave, dayNightCycle, fairground, powerGrid, enemyRoster`; `secureWave` **12**), which retires the predecessor’s hardest constraint: the shared `(secureWave + 2)` tick budget at `:349` cannot block a run-to-secure here, so the firewalled line should not need touching at all. 🔗 **The contract-defining chain is already complete and deterministic IN THE BROWSER — this slice sockets it, it does not design it, so zero operations need inventing (ERA-SOCKET LAW / Mistake #14):** `FerrisWheel.damage()` drops `spinning` on the **first hit, not on death** → `Game.ts:5894` `syncFerrisWheelPower()` mirrors that onto the graph via `set-node-online` **from the sim tick at `:2593`**, not a render path → the 24 W producer going offline starves both 6 W pavilion lamp consumers, so `fairgroundCoverageSources()` (`:5337`) drops them → and `Game.ts:4848` makes `autoSecureWaveForRun()` `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` while the wheel is stopped. **A stopped dynamo means the run can never be secured** — a real agent choice in vocabulary the contract already declares. ⛔ **THE HEADLINE IS FIREWALLED, WHICH IS THE WHOLE DESIGN OF THE MASTER.** Unlike class #5, this leaf may **NOT