tasks/BACKLOG.md:3645:- 🔺 **F-1475-1 (s1475, MEASURED) — THE FAIRGROUND SOCKET MASTER WAS JOINTLY UNSATISFIABLE, AND THE RUNNER STOPPED EXACTLY WHERE IT WAS TOLD TO.** OWNER DESIGN FORK; nothing merged, nothing lost. ⚡ **WHAT HAPPENED:** run `20260806-052014-lane-a`, **124,606 tokens, ZERO repo changes**, lane `lane/a` left clean at `c47867388` (`ahead=0`), no gates run because there was no implementation to gate. The done-move is renamed `stopped-nomode-wall-s1475-*` so no later fire reads it as drainable. 🚪 **THE WALL, RE-DERIVED FROM THE CODE RATHER THAN INHERITED FROM THE RUNNER REPORT — the `HeadlessContractSim` constructor has exactly TWO doors and `e3-fairground` fails BOTH.** Door 1 rejects a requested mode the contract does not declare (`if (boot.mode && !mode) throw`), and **`e3-fairground` declares no `modes` field at all** — measured across the whole E3 contract file: `e3-blackout-ridge` undefined, `e3-moth-season` undefined, `e3-canyon-works` **one `escort` mode**, `e3-fairground` undefined. Door 2 rejects unsupported contracts when no mode is present (`if (!SUPPORTED_CONTRACTS.has(this.contractId) && !mode) throw`), and **`e3-fairground` is the one E3 contract absent from that set** — `e3-blackout-ridge`, `e3-moth-season` and `e3-canyon-works` are all admitted, **which is precisely how all three predecessor era-sockets were provable at all.** ➡️ **So fairground was never "the cheapest socket in the class"; it was the only BLOCKED one, and the property that blocked it is the one thing the authoring fire never probed.** 🔍 **THE MASTER’S ACCEPTANCE PATH CITED A MECHANISM THAT DOES NOT EXIST.** It told the runner to prove the socket *"through the declared-`mode` path that bypasses the support gate"* and to **reuse** the census spec’s *"forced generic diagnostic"* run for fairground. There is no such run: the string `fairground` appears **exactly ONCE** in `e2e/er01-e3-census.spec.ts` — inside the `SOCKET_GAPS` record, cited by content per F-1310-1 — and that file constructs **no** `HeadlessContractSim` for it. The two `mode: escort` constructions in that spec belong to `e3-canyon-works`. **The master therefore demanded a headless proof while its own NO #3 forbade the only construction path an unadmitted contract has.** ✅ **THE RUNNER WAS RIGHT, AND THE MASTER PRE-AUTHORIZED THIS OUTCOME IN THE SAME SENTENCE:** *"If it turns out no such path can drive your assertions without admitting the contract, STOP and report it as a finding — that is a genuine design fork about what admission means, and it belongs to the owner, not to this run."* That is a well-written stop condition doing its job; **the cost of the defect was one run, not a corrupted merge**, and that is the whole value of writing stop conditions into masters. ⭐ **WHAT s1474 GOT RIGHT, RECORDED SO THE NEXT AUTHOR DOES NOT OVER-CORRECT:** its browser-chain trace verified sound (`FerrisWheel.damage()` drops `spinning` on first hit → `syncFerrisWheelPower()` mirrors it via `set-node-online` from the sim tick → the 24 W producer starves both 6 W pavilion lamps → coverage drops → `autoSecureWaveForRun()` goes `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`), as did its measurements that `twist.powerGrid` and `twist.dayNightCycle` are **already** socketed and that fairground has **no baron**. The socket SCOPE — extracting a headlessly-constructible Fair Wheel core out of `src/entities/FerrisWheel.ts` — remains sound and re-usable the moment the proof path is ruled on. 💡 **THE REUSABLE CLASS, and it is a new one: the master checked exhaustively that the SUBJECT was ready and never checked that the INSTRUMENT could be CONSTRUCTED.** Every probe it wrote asked about the wheel, the twist keys, the tick budget, the baron, the safe-dupe trap — all about the contents of the harness. **None asked whether the harness door opens for this contract.** ➡️ **Authoring rule earned here: an era-socket master must prove the harness can be INSTANTIATED for its target before it specifies one line of what to do inside it** — one construction probe, or one grep of `SUPPORTED_CONTRACTS` for the contract id, would have caught this before 124,606 tokens were spent. 🔺 **THE OWNER QUESTION — one word, and it unblocks the last E3 era-socket:** is there a **diagnostics-only** construction path that is explicitly **NOT** an admission? **RECOMMENDED (c):** a boot flag (e.g. `diagnostic: true`) that bypasses the support gate for MEASUREMENT while leaving `SUPPORTED_CONTRACTS` — the playability CLAIM — untouched, so the census headline stays **AGENT-READY 3 of 4** and the contract stays rejected until the crowd half is ruled on. **REJECTED BY THIS FIRE, with reasons: (a)** admitting `e3-fairground`, because admission asserts an agent can PLAY a contract whose advertised crowd-flock escort objective still has no consumer anywhere (`twist.fairground.crowdFlocks` sits in `DECLARED_INERT_PATHS` deliberately); **(b)** authoring a `modes` entry into contract data, which is inventing vocabulary to fit a harness — **Mistake #14, reject-do-not-stretch.** ⛔ **DO NOT RE-QUEUE THE MASTER UNCHANGED** — an identical retry of a premise already proven false is forbidden (§7.5); leaf `e3-fairground-socket` is now `blocked` / `blockClass: owner-fork` and `drain-block-check` STOPs on it.
