tasks/BACKLOG.md:3676:- ✅ **MILK SHIFT `milk/motor-socket` (2026-08-06, attended) — E4 ERA-SOCKET ATTEMPT: THE MANIFEST HALF SHIPPED, THE HEADLESS HALF IS BLOCKED BY ONE PROPERTY OF ONE FILE, AND THE CENSUS WAS WRONG ABOUT WHICH MECHANICS ARE INERT.** Branch `milk/motor-socket`, review `reviews/milk-motor-socket.md`; touches `src/agent/MechanicsManifest.ts`, `e2e/er01-e4-census.spec.ts`, `docs/bench/e4-readiness-census.md`. 🎯 **THE MEASUREMENT THAT REDIRECTED THE SHIFT:** three of the four Motor mechanics have **zero readers** in `src/` outside type declarations and two string registries (`convoyRoute`/`restStops`, `wildDerricks`/`outhouseGeyser`, `salvageHulks`/`sleeper`/`unmarkedWagon`) — socketing them would have meant WRITING the mechanic, so they stay rejected and their findings stand. **But `tileParams.orbitSpawn` is consumed in every plain browser boot**: `Game.ts:808` constructs `LandYachtBossSystem` unconditionally, `Game.ts:2549` updates it every tick, and `LandYachtBossSystem.ts:256-277` reads `center/radius/angularSpeed` to drive the Land Yacht around the ORBIT road. Under AP-11 (**declared AND consumed**) the ORBIT road was always owed a manifest entry; it now has **five consumer-derived rules and ZERO invented operations** (`land_yacht_orbit/acts/head_loot/crane/dread`). ⭐ **Gated on DATA, not contract id** — `twist.baron?.variantId === 'land_yacht' && tile.orbitSpawn`, mirroring the browser's own gate at `Game.ts:2545`; both E3 precedents hardcode `contract.id`, which AP-11 amendment 1 calls "a manifest hole". 🚫 **The four `orbitSpawn` fields nothing reads (`lapsBeforePeel`, `peelSpeed`, `telegraphSeconds`, `peelPoints`) stay OUT, and the spec now ASSERTS their absence** so a later author cannot mint them by accident. ⛔ **F-ER01-E4-5 (NEW) — THE SOCKET'S BLOCKER, AND IT IS A NEW CLASS:** `LandYachtBossSystem.ts:56` builds a sprite in a **field initializer** → `TextureLoader` → `ImageLoader` → **`document is not defined`** under the Node harness (`vite