e the summary line `DATA-GAP: 4 of 4` matches too. Same shape as s1478's "FOUR E2 profiles not five". 📐 **A record correction:** the F-1470-1 note above says `CrawlerBossSystem` calls `document.querySelector` "from its constructor and every `update()`" — measured, **the constructor is DOM-free and the call sits in `syncPresentation`, which `step()` bypasses**; its other stated reasons may hold, this one does not. 🧪 **Gates:** tsc **rc=0** · build **rc=0** (`✓ built in 1.17s`) · `er01-e2/e3/e4/e5/e6-census` + `drill-yard-manifest` **42 passed / 0 failed / 3.5m**, both projects, `--workers=1` · manifest byte-stable across two derivations · blast radius measured **0** `land_yacht` rules on the other three E4 contracts and all five E1 fixture contracts. **`SUPPORTED_CONTRACTS`, `bench-seeds.json` and the headline `AGENT-READY 0 of 4` deliberately UNCHANGED — the contract is NOT admitted.** **GATE: closes when F-ER01-E4-5 lands and `e4-dust-flats` is socketed + admitted with its determinism pair.** ⤵️ **DRAINED + MERGED `d66bdbe3` s1496 — the THIRD member of the milk pile to land, and the drain order's one explicit instruction was carried out.** Gated on the MERGED tree in detached worktree `gate-s1496` (§3.0b), all `--workers=1` on Node 26.4.0: **tsc rc=0 · build rc=0 in 1.17s · own spec `er01-e4-census` 8/8 · adjacent 68/68 · `test:node-guards` rc=0, zero `not ok`** (mandatory — touches `src/agent/`). Transcript `artifacts/s1496-drain-gate.txt`. ✅ **THE CONTROL RUN ON CLEAN MAIN VINDICATES THE SLICE, WHICH IS WHY IT WAS ORDERED:** at clean main `6f8deccbe` `agent-view.spec.ts` is **4 failed / 4 passed**; on the merged tree it is **the SAME 4** (`:264` + `:297`, both projects) with **12 passed**. **Identical fingerprint on both sides ⇒ the slice introduces no red**, and F-MOTOR-1's root cause is confirmed exactly as the review states. 🟥 **F-1496-1 (NEW, against the review's own evidence) — IT UNDER-COUNTS ITS RED BY HALF.** The review says *"2 desktop reds"* and *"the s